WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.866 --> 00:00:01.533
- Pete, Joe.

00:00:01.634 --> 00:00:02.601
Congratulations.

00:00:02.701 --> 00:00:03.869
You've made it into the final.

00:00:03.936 --> 00:00:05.071
Now we're sending
you back to your home

00:00:05.138 --> 00:00:06.773
forges where you
will have to forge

00:00:06.839 --> 00:00:08.307
an iconic blade from history.

00:00:08.407 --> 00:00:10.543
Are you ready to see
what that weapon is?

00:00:10.643 --> 00:00:11.510
 Oh, yeah.

00:00:11.577 --> 00:00:12.245
 Yes.

00:00:12.345 --> 00:00:14.780
Absolutely.

00:00:14.880 --> 00:00:17.150
 The pandat.

00:00:17.217 --> 00:00:18.484
 Oh!

00:00:18.584 --> 00:00:20.219
WIL (VOICEOVER): The pandat
is a two-handed sword carried

00:00:20.286 --> 00:00:22.255
into battle by the
Dayaks, a group

00:00:22.321 --> 00:00:24.557
of tribes that lived
on the island of Borneo

00:00:24.657 --> 00:00:26.058
for thousands of years.

00:00:26.159 --> 00:00:28.861
Though most Dayak weapons
doubled as useful tools,

00:00:28.927 --> 00:00:30.964
the pandat was only used in war.

00:00:31.064 --> 00:00:33.566
Forged from iron, the pandat
features an angled blade

00:00:33.633 --> 00:00:36.302
and can be swung
downwards with two hands.

00:00:36.369 --> 00:00:38.604
An iron cross piece was
inserted through a hole

00:00:38.671 --> 00:00:41.474
at the end of the handle,
protecting the user's hand.

00:00:41.574 --> 00:00:42.909
The blade was
sometimes decorated

00:00:43.009 --> 00:00:44.878
with hair or rattan plant.

00:00:44.944 --> 00:00:47.180
Until the early 20th
century, Dayak raiders

00:00:47.246 --> 00:00:50.216
plundered coastal settlements
for resources, money,

00:00:50.316 --> 00:00:52.652
and even enemy heads,
proving just how

00:00:52.752 --> 00:00:54.620
deadly this weapon could be.

00:00:54.687 --> 00:00:55.688
Good luck bladesmiths.

00:00:55.788 --> 00:00:56.790
We'll see you in five days.

00:01:03.095 --> 00:01:05.631 line:7%
 This is home, Jenks, Oklahoma.

00:01:05.698 --> 00:01:06.765 line:7%
It's going to be hot.

00:01:06.832 --> 00:01:08.400
It's going to be humid.

00:01:08.467 --> 00:01:11.571
But I'm not worried about
anything other than an accident

00:01:11.637 --> 00:01:14.107
or the unforeseen.

00:01:14.207 --> 00:01:16.075
I mean, I have never
seen this blade.

00:01:16.175 --> 00:01:18.010
I've never even heard of it.

00:01:18.077 --> 00:01:20.412
A little apprehensive
about building it.

00:01:20.479 --> 00:01:23.549
Five days-- it seems
like a lot of time.

00:01:23.649 --> 00:01:25.585
But to build a piece
like this, it's going

00:01:25.652 --> 00:01:29.255
to be really, really hard.

00:01:29.322 --> 00:01:29.789
Come on.

00:01:29.856 --> 00:01:30.823
Stay with me.

00:01:30.923 --> 00:01:32.758
Don't-- don't power out on me.

00:01:32.859 --> 00:01:34.593
What's going on?

00:01:34.660 --> 00:01:36.162
Oh, wow.

00:01:36.229 --> 00:01:38.230
I haven't seen it rain this
hard in a long time, y'all.

00:01:38.330 --> 00:01:41.400
I mean, this is kind of intense.

00:01:41.500 --> 00:01:43.602
Oh, [bleep].

00:01:43.702 --> 00:01:44.637
Oh, [bleep].

00:01:44.704 --> 00:01:45.671
OK.

00:01:45.771 --> 00:01:47.006
Yeah, boys.

00:01:47.073 --> 00:01:47.774
Damn it!

00:01:51.110 --> 00:01:52.912
Go, go, go.

00:01:53.012 --> 00:01:53.912
Stay where you're at.

00:01:53.979 --> 00:01:54.714
Do not move.

00:01:57.717 --> 00:02:00.252 line:0%
Midway through day one,
everything's going great

00:02:00.352 --> 00:02:03.222 line:7%
and boom, amazing storm hits.

00:02:03.288 --> 00:02:05.124
I mean, this thing was unreal.

00:02:05.224 --> 00:02:06.292
There was some damage done.

00:02:06.392 --> 00:02:07.727
We had a lot of trees down.

00:02:07.794 --> 00:02:09.762
Took out, of course, the
meter and the power lines.

00:02:09.862 --> 00:02:12.932
Doesn't look like we're going
to get power back anytime soon.

00:02:12.999 --> 00:02:14.233
So we're going to
get a generator.

00:02:14.299 --> 00:02:15.567
We're going to get it pumped up.

00:02:15.668 --> 00:02:17.303
We're gonna get power and
juice back in the shop.

00:02:17.403 --> 00:02:19.205
And then we're
gonna move forward.

00:02:19.272 --> 00:02:20.740
[generator starting]

00:02:20.807 --> 00:02:22.074
Yay!

00:02:22.175 --> 00:02:24.377
We have power.

00:02:24.443 --> 00:02:26.713
This was a pretty good setback.

00:02:26.813 --> 00:02:28.247
It's reality check.

00:02:28.347 --> 00:02:30.383
You go, hey, you sure you
got what it takes to do this?

00:02:32.885 --> 00:02:37.790 line:0%
 Today is day three, and
I've been told it's Saturday.

00:02:37.856 --> 00:02:38.891
There's gonna be a cutting test.

00:02:38.958 --> 00:02:40.059
There's gonna be
a strength test.

00:02:40.126 --> 00:02:41.694
There's going to be
a KEAL test, too.

00:02:41.761 --> 00:02:46.032
So I want to draw my spine back
so it's a little softer so it's

00:02:46.132 --> 00:02:47.500
got a little bit of flex.

00:02:47.600 --> 00:02:51.203
So I rigged up kind of
an ancient way to do it.

00:02:51.303 --> 00:02:54.139
I've dug a trench to
keep the edge cool,

00:02:54.206 --> 00:02:56.176
so it won't get soft.

00:02:59.345 --> 00:03:00.780
I've really been fighting
the wind with it.

00:03:00.846 --> 00:03:05.384
But as fast as you get it
warmed up, it cools down.

00:03:05.451 --> 00:03:07.687
I also have to keep
water in the trench.

00:03:07.753 --> 00:03:11.424
When you've got a very hot torch
blasting against the water,

00:03:11.490 --> 00:03:14.193
it evaporates rather quickly.

00:03:14.259 --> 00:03:15.695
I'm not sure I'm
going to get it done.

00:03:18.197 --> 00:03:20.132 line:0%
 Day four, either
we top the hill

00:03:20.199 --> 00:03:21.400 line:7%
or we roll down another one.

00:03:21.500 --> 00:03:23.636
Today's a make or break
day for this blade.

00:03:23.703 --> 00:03:27.674
We're going to quench this
thing and hope for the best.

00:03:27.774 --> 00:03:29.342
And hopefully your
best is good enough.

00:03:35.215 --> 00:03:37.450
Doing this is about as
nerve wracking as it gets.

00:03:40.820 --> 00:03:42.889
You just want everything
to go nice and smooth.

00:03:48.560 --> 00:03:54.399
It did harden, but I got
crazy-ass warpage right there.

00:03:54.500 --> 00:03:57.002
It's a bit of a
kick in the pants.

00:03:57.069 --> 00:03:58.304
We're running out of time.

00:03:58.371 --> 00:03:59.505
Grind, grind, grind.

00:03:59.571 --> 00:04:00.673
That's what it's
going to come down to.

00:04:00.740 --> 00:04:02.642
And hopefully we'll
get that warp out.

00:04:06.245 --> 00:04:09.181
 Bladesmiths, this
is the sharpness test.

00:04:09.248 --> 00:04:11.317
To see how sharp
your weapons are,

00:04:11.384 --> 00:04:13.553
I will attempt to cut
through these web of ropes

00:04:13.619 --> 00:04:15.687
with three identical strikes.

00:04:15.754 --> 00:04:18.591
If they're sharp, I
should meet no resistance.

00:04:18.658 --> 00:04:20.058
Joey, you're up first.
You ready?

00:04:20.159 --> 00:04:20.793
 Let's do it.

00:04:35.274 --> 00:04:36.509
 Well, Joe.

00:04:36.575 --> 00:04:38.477
All the weight is at
the tip of the blade.

00:04:38.544 --> 00:04:41.647
So when I come down, it
wants to draw me forward.

00:04:41.747 --> 00:04:45.418
And the recovery is a little
bit harder on the way back.

00:04:45.484 --> 00:04:47.319
You have a sharp
edge over here that I

00:04:47.386 --> 00:04:49.622
almost met no resistance.

00:04:49.689 --> 00:04:54.259
Overall sir, your
blade will cut.

00:04:54.326 --> 00:04:55.127
Pete, you're up next.

00:04:55.194 --> 00:04:55.995
You ready?

00:04:56.062 --> 00:04:56.796
 Yes, sir.

00:04:56.863 --> 00:04:57.563
Let's do this.

00:05:06.272 --> 00:05:07.140
 OK, Pete.

00:05:07.240 --> 00:05:08.407
It is a sharp blade.

00:05:08.474 --> 00:05:10.409
The balance is light.

00:05:10.475 --> 00:05:11.476
You have a lighter blade, here.

00:05:11.577 --> 00:05:14.246
It's not as heavy
to pull forward.

00:05:14.347 --> 00:05:15.848
It's a good job.

00:05:15.915 --> 00:05:19.718
The only issue I have is that I
kind of ran out of handle here.

00:05:19.818 --> 00:05:22.755
I would have liked to see a
little pommel here, or probably

00:05:22.855 --> 00:05:24.890
even a longer handle
so it's easier

00:05:24.957 --> 00:05:28.728
to control and not feel like
I'm at the end of my rope,

00:05:28.828 --> 00:05:29.729
so to say.

00:05:29.795 --> 00:05:32.731
Overall, this weapon,
sir, will cut.

00:05:32.798 --> 00:05:34.167
 Thank you.

00:05:34.267 --> 00:05:37.736
 All right bladesmiths,
next up is a kill test.

00:05:37.803 --> 00:05:39.572
Now the pandat was a
weapon used by head

00:05:39.639 --> 00:05:41.073
hunting tribes in Borneo.

00:05:41.173 --> 00:05:44.544
To see how lethal your weapon
is, I will take your pandat

00:05:44.644 --> 00:05:48.513
and I will deliver one
blow to this carcass.

00:05:48.580 --> 00:05:50.483
Let's see how much damage
your weapon can do.

00:05:50.550 --> 00:05:51.850
Joe, you're up first.
You ready?

00:05:51.917 --> 00:05:52.618
 Bring it.

00:05:52.719 --> 00:05:53.353
 Let's do it.

00:06:01.327 --> 00:06:02.361
OK, John.

00:06:02.428 --> 00:06:04.464
The balance feels
so forward-heavy

00:06:04.564 --> 00:06:08.034
that when you slice through this
carcass, it pulled me into it

00:06:08.134 --> 00:06:10.536
and cut cleanly all
the way through.

00:06:10.636 --> 00:06:13.039
This weapon, sir, will kill.

00:06:13.139 --> 00:06:13.772
Good job.

00:06:13.839 --> 00:06:14.940
 Thank you.

00:06:15.007 --> 00:06:15.741
 Pete, you're up next.

00:06:15.808 --> 00:06:16.342
You ready?

00:06:16.409 --> 00:06:17.110
 Yes I am.

00:06:29.422 --> 00:06:30.689
 OK, Pete.

00:06:30.790 --> 00:06:32.758
The difference with your
blade is that it's light.

00:06:32.859 --> 00:06:35.961
And because it's light, I
can use velocity to help

00:06:36.028 --> 00:06:37.897
cut through this carcass.

00:06:37.997 --> 00:06:40.666
This weapon, sir, will kill.

00:06:40.766 --> 00:06:41.333
Good job.

00:06:41.400 --> 00:06:42.501
 Thank you.

00:06:42.568 --> 00:06:43.502
 All right, gentlemen.

00:06:43.569 --> 00:06:44.870
This is the strength test.

00:06:44.937 --> 00:06:47.506
To test the strength and
durability of your blades,

00:06:47.572 --> 00:06:49.074
we're going to hook
them into our machine

00:06:49.174 --> 00:06:52.611
here, which is going to chop
into this bundle of sugar cane.

00:06:52.711 --> 00:06:54.914
Now, if your blades
are tempered properly,

00:06:55.014 --> 00:06:57.616
they should cut into the
cane without a problem.

00:06:57.683 --> 00:07:00.285
If not, we might get
them to bend, warp--

00:07:00.385 --> 00:07:01.653
well, we'll see what happens.

00:07:01.720 --> 00:07:03.288
Joe, you're already
rigged up on the machine.

00:07:03.388 --> 00:07:04.790
You ready to go?
- Let's go.

00:07:04.890 --> 00:07:05.324
 All right.

00:07:05.424 --> 00:07:06.692
Let's do it.

00:07:06.793 --> 00:07:08.727
 All right, Joe.

00:07:08.794 --> 00:07:10.930
3, 2, 1.

00:07:15.000 --> 00:07:15.734
All right.

00:07:15.801 --> 00:07:16.768
So, Joe.

00:07:16.835 --> 00:07:18.838
Now when I pull this
out of the machine,

00:07:18.905 --> 00:07:20.373
there's a bit of
a bend right here

00:07:20.440 --> 00:07:23.609
in the ricasso, kind of a
gap right along the edge

00:07:23.676 --> 00:07:25.178
of the blade in the guard.

00:07:25.244 --> 00:07:26.579
 It had that warp
when it got here.

00:07:26.645 --> 00:07:30.148
 It had that warp
when it got here?

00:07:30.215 --> 00:07:31.383
 It was actually offset.

00:07:31.450 --> 00:07:32.484
It's got a little
bit of a twist--

00:07:32.551 --> 00:07:34.020
maybe a five degree twist.

00:07:34.086 --> 00:07:35.887
I couldn't get it out
whenever I built it.

00:07:35.988 --> 00:07:39.091
 Well, it may have gotten
bigger during that test.

00:07:39.157 --> 00:07:41.393
Overall, the edge held up fine.

00:07:41.493 --> 00:07:43.863
No damage whatsoever.

00:07:43.963 --> 00:07:45.297
It's got a good shape.

00:07:45.364 --> 00:07:46.398
Good job.

00:07:46.499 --> 00:07:47.233
 Thanks, sir.

00:07:47.299 --> 00:07:48.166
 All right, Pete.

00:07:48.233 --> 00:07:49.034
You're all locked in.

00:07:49.101 --> 00:07:50.135
Ready for this?

00:07:50.235 --> 00:07:51.002
 I am.

00:07:51.069 --> 00:07:52.505
 All right.

00:07:52.571 --> 00:07:55.040
 All right, Pete.

00:07:55.107 --> 00:07:57.677
3, 2, 1.

00:08:03.850 --> 00:08:04.983
All right, Pete.

00:08:05.050 --> 00:08:07.820
You can actually see how
much this blade flexed when

00:08:07.887 --> 00:08:11.791
it went into the cane and
came back to true, which

00:08:11.857 --> 00:08:13.559
is always what I want to see.

00:08:13.625 --> 00:08:16.428
Definitely sharp,
well put together.

00:08:16.495 --> 00:08:17.863
Feels good.

00:08:17.930 --> 00:08:18.797
Well done, Pete.

00:08:18.897 --> 00:08:19.765
 Thank you.

00:08:22.568 --> 00:08:25.303
 Gentlemen, this is one of
the tightest competitions

00:08:25.404 --> 00:08:26.671
that we've had.

00:08:26.772 --> 00:08:29.375
It's exactly what we want
from our bladesmiths.

00:08:29.475 --> 00:08:30.943
It was a difficult decision.

00:08:31.043 --> 00:08:33.679
But that final
decision has been made.

00:08:33.779 --> 00:08:35.715
And the Forged in
Fire champion is--

00:08:40.152 --> 00:08:41.420
Pete, congratulations.

00:08:41.520 --> 00:08:44.489
You are the Forged
in Fire champion.

00:08:44.556 --> 00:08:47.593
Joe, please surrender
your weapon.

00:08:50.829 --> 00:08:52.831
 This experience has taught
me, like many things in life,

00:08:52.898 --> 00:08:53.833
to try.

00:08:53.900 --> 00:08:54.600
Dare to fail.

00:08:54.700 --> 00:08:56.702
If you fail, so what?

00:08:56.802 --> 00:08:58.137
Feeling kind of
disappointed right now.

00:08:58.237 --> 00:09:00.306
But at least I tried.

00:09:04.043 --> 00:09:04.877
 Pete, congratulations.

00:09:04.944 --> 00:09:06.512
You are the Forged
in Fire champion

00:09:06.612 --> 00:09:08.914
and will be receiving
that check for 10 grand.

00:09:08.981 --> 00:09:09.815
Good job.

00:09:09.915 --> 00:09:10.483
Thank you.

00:09:10.583 --> 00:09:13.085
[applause]

00:09:14.586 --> 00:09:17.156
 Pete, what I really
liked about your blade,

00:09:17.222 --> 00:09:19.725 line:0%
amongst many things, is I
wanted to grab that thing

00:09:19.792 --> 00:09:21.160 line:7%
and cut something with it.

00:09:21.227 --> 00:09:23.396 line:7%
And when I felt it--

00:09:23.496 --> 00:09:25.564 line:0%
I mean, it gives you the
woo to strike, you know?

00:09:25.664 --> 00:09:28.334
It really does want to cut.

00:09:28.434 --> 00:09:29.902
 How you feeling
right now, Pete?

00:09:30.002 --> 00:09:31.670
 Feel pretty good.

00:09:31.770 --> 00:09:34.840
I'm feeling like I could just
roll on the floor and bust

00:09:34.941 --> 00:09:35.574
out laughing.

00:09:35.641 --> 00:09:37.142
It feels real good.

00:09:37.209 --> 00:09:38.577
Feels real good to win.

00:09:38.644 --> 00:09:41.880
I'm going home the
Forged in Fire champion.

00:09:41.981 --> 00:09:44.283
And I know all 24
of my grandkids

00:09:44.350 --> 00:09:46.953
are going to be
excited for Grandpa.

